<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-AUSTRALIAN P-NOTES - Tenders total A$60.0 mln.</title>
<headline>RTRS-AUSTRALIAN P-NOTES - Tenders total A$60.0 mln.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian promissory note issuers came to the market for a total of A$60.0 million on Monday.</p>
<p>McDonald's Corp's Australian unit was the largest issuer on the day selling A$30 million of one-month paper.</p>
<p>ICI Australia Ltd sold A$20.0 million worth of one-month p-notes at 5.5 points over bill. Incitec Ltd sold A$10.0 million of its one-month paper.</p>
<p>At 11.15 a.m. (0015 GMT), March 90-day bank bill futures were trading at 94.35, down three points on the day.</p>
